"""Guild main quest lines (v75 story engine data; deobf/GUILD_EXPANSION_SPEC.md §10).

A story is a list of chapters. A chapter is offered by the guild leader (hub node 720) once the player has the
level, the contracts (rep) and the previous chapter; accepting starts its first step. Each step is a scene at one
NPC (an existing conversation file or a new character added by the story) that plays when the step is current and
its `need` conditions hold; an option with go=None finishes the step (next step, or the chapter end with its
promotion). `jump` names another step of the same chapter.

Beat:  {'t': text | [(cond, text), ..., (None, default)], 'o': [option, ...]}
Option: {'t': text, 'go': beat index | None (finish step) | 'hold' (end, step stays), 'a': actions, 'c': conds,
         'jump': step label}
Text markup: [BLUE]..[] narration.  Choice variables: ekg_c_<g>_<key>.
"""

